  "security_implications": "The chunk latches rdata (potentially secret/uninitialized register data) into rdata_q and a sticky-like error status into error_q (though error_q can change on response phase). rdata_q holds stale data while a_ack is high; if it is read during that phase, a secret could leak. error_q is used to signal errors; if it is misinterpreted or never cleared (e.g., external logic treats any error as fatal and does not allow recovery), transient errors could cause denial-of-service or mask subsequent security events. The adapter is a gatekeeper between bus and registers; any failure in its error handling or data staging could affect integrity/confidentiality of the device’s register state.",
